---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import IntelligencePageLead from '../../../components/intelligence/IntelligencePageLead.astro';

const path = '/intelligence/hardware/deliverable-megawatts/';
const title = 'From Paper Gigawatts to Deliverable Megawatts';
const description = 'August 2026 AI infrastructure field note: a proof ladder for separating announced capacity from operating compute.';
const published = '2026-09-01';

const proofLadder = [
  { label: 'Announced', note: 'A target enters the public record.' },
  { label: 'Controlled', note: 'Land and power rights become specific.' },
  { label: 'Contracted', note: 'Customers and capital accept obligations.' },
  { label: 'Building', note: 'Permits, equipment, and civil work are visible.' },
  { label: 'Commissioned', note: 'The system is tested as one machine.' },
  { label: 'Operating', note: 'Compute is live, accepted, and measurable.' },
] as const;

const schema = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'Article',
    '@id': `https://iamrobin.ai${path}#article`,
    headline: title,
    description,
    url: `https://iamrobin.ai${path}`,
    datePublished: published,
    dateModified: published,
    inLanguage: 'en',
    author: { '@id': 'https://iamrobin.ai/#person' },
    isPartOf: { '@id': 'https://iamrobin.ai/intelligence/#page' },
  },
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
    itemListElement: [
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Intelligence', item: 'https://iamrobin.ai/intelligence/' },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'AI Hardware', item: 'https://iamrobin.ai/intelligence/hardware/' },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 3, name: title, item: `https://iamrobin.ai${path}` },
    ],
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`${title} — Intelligence — Robin Xie`}
  {description}
  {path}
  type="article"
  {schema}
>
  <IntelligencePageLead
    lens="Flow / August 2026"
    title="Deliverable megawatts."
    line="The announcement is the beginning of the evidence, not the end."
  />

  <article class="field-note shell">
    <header class="field-note__header">
      <p class="field-note__date"><time datetime={published}>September 1, 2026</time> · 8 minute field note</p>
      <h2>From paper gigawatts to operating compute</h2>
      <p class="field-note__lede">
        August's strongest AI-infrastructure signal was not another record-sized project. It was the widening distance between capacity that has been named and capacity that can actually arrive on time.
      </p>
    </header>

    <ol class="proof-ladder" aria-label="AI infrastructure proof ladder">
      {proofLadder.map((step, index) => (
        <li>
          <span>{String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
          <strong>{step.label}</strong>
          <small>{step.note}</small>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ol>

    <section>
      <p class="eyebrow">01 / The denominator</p>
      <h2>Pipeline is not production.</h2>
      <p>
        Global Energy Monitor counted <strong>189 GW</strong> of U.S. gas-fired capacity in development specifically for data-center load in its August release. Only <strong>16.9 GW</strong> was under construction: about <strong>8.9%</strong> of that pipeline.
      </p>
      <p>
        More than half of the relevant projects did not name a turbine or engine supplier, and nearly one quarter did not name a start year. Those are not failed projects. They are projects whose delivery evidence is still incomplete.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <p class="eyebrow">02 / Geography</p>
      <h2>Power is pulling compute away from the city.</h2>
      <p>
        JLL's EMEA mid-year report places hyperscale sites planned for 2026–2028 an average of <strong>175 km</strong> from major hub cities, compared with <strong>46 km</strong> for facilities completed during 2022–2025. Greenfield sites rise from <strong>8%</strong> to <strong>39%</strong> of the 2026–2028 pipeline.
      </p>
      <p>
        Latency still matters. But for training and other location-flexible workloads, a credible power date can now outweigh proximity to the traditional hub.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <p class="eyebrow">03 / Contracts</p>
      <h2>A contract can move a project up the ladder. It cannot skip the ladder.</h2>
      <p>
        OpenAI and NVIDIA describe approximately <strong>8 IT-GW</strong> at PORTS-Pike under a 20-year lease structure, with NVIDIA investing <strong>$1.5 billion</strong> and providing credit support for the initial <strong>4.25 IT-GW</strong>. The first <strong>800 MW</strong> is expected in 2028.
      </p>
      <p>
        That is stronger evidence than an uncontracted target. It is still development-stage capacity: OpenAI says later delivery depends on infrastructure, permits, environmental reviews, and financing. Payments begin as completed capacity becomes available.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <p class="eyebrow">04 / Capital structure</p>
      <h2>Operating assets make future capacity easier to finance.</h2>
      <p>
        SK Telecom's proposed SK Horizon combines eight operating data centers with Ulsan and Guro facilities under construction and a target of <strong>318 MW</strong>. KKR and the IMM consortium agreed to invest <strong>KRW 3.08 trillion</strong>, subject to the transaction's approvals and expected 2027 formation.
      </p>
      <p>
        The useful distinction is inside the same announcement: operating sites, construction-stage sites, a platform target, and separate multi-gigawatt aspirations are four different evidence states.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <p class="eyebrow">05 / Bridge power</p>
      <h2>Time-to-power is becoming a product.</h2>
      <p>
        Aggreko's August Form F-1 reports a <strong>17 GW</strong> global power-and-temperature-control fleet. Its data-center revenue rose from <strong>$96 million</strong> in fiscal 2023 to <strong>$391 million</strong> in fiscal 2025.
      </p>
      <p>
        Mobile generation and modular cooling can bring a commercial date forward while a grid connection waits. They do not erase fuel, emissions, utilization, or migration risk. Bridge power is useful because the permanent bottleneck remains real.
      </p>
    </section>

    <aside class="field-note__rule">
      <p class="eyebrow">The August rule</p>
      <blockquote>
        Never value a paper gigawatt as an operating megawatt. Ask which rung it has reached, what evidence moved it there, and what can still stop it.
      </blockquote>
    </aside>

    <section>
      <p class="eyebrow">06 / What to watch next</p>
      <h2>The upgrade tests are observable.</h2>
      <ul class="watch-list">
        <li>Named equipment suppliers and reserved manufacturing slots.</li>
        <li>Executed interconnection, fuel, land, and customer agreements.</li>
        <li>Permits, financing close, and notice to proceed.</li>
        <li>Construction progress, energization, commissioning, and customer acceptance.</li>
        <li>Operating power, utilization, reliability, and unit economics.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Job postings from OpenAI and Anthropic reinforce the shape of the work—power, land, silicon, fiber, capital, construction, commissioning, and operations—but prove hiring intent only. They do not move any project up the ladder.
      </p>
    </section>

    <footer class="field-note__sources">
      <p class="eyebrow">Sources / refreshed September 1, 2026</p>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="https://globalenergymonitor.org/research/us-gas-power-proposals-tied-data-centers-nearly-double-six-months">Global Energy Monitor — U.S. gas power proposals tied to data centers</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://www.jll.com/en-uk/insights/emea-data-centre-report">JLL — EMEA data centre mid-year 2026 report</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://openai.com/index/openai-joins-ports-pike-project/">OpenAI — PORTS-Pike project agreement</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://nvidianews.nvidia.com/news/nvidia-guarantees-sb-energy-s-ports-pike-technology-campus-in-ohio-to-exclusively-host-nvidia-ai-compute">NVIDIA — PORTS-Pike investment and credit support</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://news.sktelecom.com/en/3290">SK Telecom — SK Horizon transaction</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2134090/000110465926100313/tmq-20260824xf1.htm">U.S. SEC — Aggreko Form F-1</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://openai.com/careers/business-development-lead-compute-strategy-us-remote/">OpenAI — Compute Strategy hiring intent</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://www.anthropic.com/careers/jobs/5013743008">Anthropic — Data Center Infrastructure hiring intent</a></li>
      </ul>
      <a class="field-note__back" href="/intelligence/hardware/">← Return to AI Hardware</a>
    </footer>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .field-note {
    max-width: 58rem;
    margin-bottom: clamp(5rem, 10vw, 9rem);
  }

  .field-note__header,
  .field-note section,
  .field-note__rule,
  .field-note__sources {
    max-width: 46rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  .field-note__date {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .field-note__header h2,
  .field-note section h2 {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
  }

  .field-note__header h2 {
    max-width: 14ch;
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 4.2rem);
    line-height: 0.98;
  }

  .field-note__lede {
    max-width: 38rem;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: clamp(1.1rem, 2.4vw, 1.45rem);
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  .proof-ladder {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(6, 1fr);
    margin: clamp(3.5rem, 8vw, 6.5rem) 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .proof-ladder li {
    position: relative;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.45rem;
    min-height: 9rem;
    padding: 1rem 0.8rem;
  }

  .proof-ladder li:not(:last-child) {
    border-right: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .proof-ladder li::after {
    position: absolute;
    right: -0.36rem;
    bottom: 1.1rem;
    z-index: 1;
    width: 0.65rem;
    height: 0.65rem;
    content: '';
    background: var(--paper);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--gold);
    border-right: 1px solid var(--gold);
    transform: rotate(45deg);
  }

  .proof-ladder li:last-child::after {
    display: none;
  }

  .proof-ladder span {
    color: var(--silver);
    font-size: 0.58rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
  }

  .proof-ladder strong {
    align-self: end;
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: clamp(0.95rem, 1.8vw, 1.2rem);
    font-weight: 400;
  }

  .proof-ladder small {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    line-height: 1.4;
  }

  .field-note section {
    margin-top: clamp(3.8rem, 8vw, 6rem);
  }

  .field-note section h2 {
    max-width: 20ch;
    margin: 0.75rem 0 1.3rem;
    font-size: clamp(1.65rem, 4vw, 2.7rem);
    line-height: 1.08;
  }

  .field-note section p,
  .field-note section li {
    font-size: clamp(1rem, 1.8vw, 1.12rem);
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  .field-note section p + p {
    margin-top: 1.1rem;
  }

  .field-note__rule {
    margin-top: clamp(4rem, 9vw, 7rem);
    padding: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 2.6rem);
    background:
      radial-gradient(circle at 85% 20%, rgba(180, 145, 93, 0.13), transparent 33%),
      rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.34);
    border: 1px solid rgba(180, 145, 93, 0.28);
  }

  .field-note__rule blockquote {
    max-width: 30ch;
    margin: 1rem 0 0;
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 4vw, 2.3rem);
    line-height: 1.25;
  }

  .watch-list {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    margin: 1.4rem 0 1.7rem;
    padding-left: 1.2rem;
  }

  .field-note__sources {
    margin-top: clamp(4.5rem, 9vw, 7rem);
    padding-top: 2rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .field-note__sources ul {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.7rem;
    margin: 1.2rem 0 2rem;
    padding-left: 1.15rem;
  }

  .field-note__sources li {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.86rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .field-note__sources a {
    color: inherit;
    text-decoration-color: var(--line);
    text-underline-offset: 0.25em;
  }

  .field-note__sources a:hover,
  .field-note__sources a:focus-visible {
    color: var(--ink);
    text-decoration-color: var(--gold);
  }

  .field-note__back {
    display: inline-block;
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    font-weight: 650;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  @media (max-width: 47.99rem) {
    .proof-ladder {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    }

    .proof-ladder li {
      min-height: 7.8rem;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    }

    .proof-ladder li:nth-child(2n) {
      border-right: 0;
    }

    .proof-ladder li:nth-last-child(-n + 2) {
      border-bottom: 0;
    }

    .proof-ladder li::after {
      display: none;
    }
  }
</style>
